  <h2>Deep Notes</h2>
  <p>History</p>
  <ul>
    <li>New LSL function integer llSetRegionPos(vector position) in Second Life Server 12.01.24.248357
The object with the script will move the root prim position to the given location. The position is any position within the region. If the position is below ground, it will be set to the ground level at that X,Y spot. The function has no delay or throttle.
    <ul>
      <li>Returns 1 if the object is successfully placed within 0.1 m of position.</li>
      <li>Returns 0 and does not move the object if position is more than 10m off region or above 4096m.</li>
      <li>Returns 0 and does not move the object if the object is dynamic (has physics enabled).</li>
      <li>Returns 0 and does not move the object if the object can not move to position due to object entry rules, prim limits, bans, etc.</li>
    </ul>
  
    </li>
  </ul>
